<section class="border-t border-line bg-app" aria-labelledby="confidence-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <h2 id="confidence-title" class="h2">
        Exact answers, only from work you can open.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5 max-w-[46ch]">
        A query either runs as written or is refused with a reason. Whatever it returns is limited to the projects the
        person, or the agent’s token, can open.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm list-none">
        <li>
          <a class="link" href="/features/project-reports">
            Reports scoped by a query or a view
            <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">
              →
            </span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="link" href="/features/mcp-ai-agents">
            Agents that search the same way
            <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">
              →
            </span>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7 rule-list">
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="h3">A typo is refused, with the fix beside it.</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          The part at fault is underlined, and the values that exist in the projects you can see appear beneath it as
          one-click replacements. An agent gets the same list back and corrects itself. Nothing is silently ignored, so
          a typo never looks like an empty result.
        </p>
        <p class="quote mt-3">status: Donee → Donee is not a valid value for status.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="h3">Only projects you can open.</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          Jordan is a member of ACME but not of OPS. When Jordan searches <code>#Unresolved</code>, the answer comes
          from ACME alone: no OPS issue appears in the list, a group count, a report figure or an exported file, and
          autocomplete suggests only values from ACME. An agent’s token can narrow its projects further.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="h3">Views follow their definition.</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          Change a view and every search that names it follows. Delete it, and a search that still names it says so.
          Views can build on views: <code>{'#{Open work} assignee: me'}</code> works even when <em>Open work</em> is
          made from another view.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="h3">A saved view is a query, not a page.</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          A view keeps a query, its sort and its columns, for you, one project or the whole organisation. Knowledge base
          articles are documents, private to the members of their project, with a search of their own.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

